[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_052267913c43cc46016a207230865c8197bd69786ff70dcddc","text":"Implemented a minimal tscircuit RP2040 breakout in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx), with local JLCPCB imports for:\n\n- [RP2040](/workspace/imports/RP2040.tsx)\n- [W25Q32JVSSIQ flash](/workspace/imports/W25Q32JVSSIQ.tsx)\n- [XC6206P332MR 3.3 V regulator](/workspace/imports/XC6206P332MR.tsx)\n\nIt includes USB-C, 3.3 V regulation, external flash, 12 MHz crystal with load caps, BOOT/RESET buttons, SWD header, breakout headers, decoupling, copper pours, and a GPIO25 LED. I did not use `routingDisabled`; verified no `routingDisabled` / `routing-disabled` strings exist outside dependencies.\n\nValidation:\n- `bun run typecheck`: passed\n- `tsci check netlist index.circuit.tsx`: passed, 0 errors/warnings\n- `tsci check placement index.circuit.tsx`: passed, 0 errors/warnings\n- `tsci build index.circuit.tsx --pcb-svgs --schematic-svgs`: produced `dist/index/circuit.json`, `dist/index/pcb.svg`, and `dist/index/schematic.svg`, but the autorouter reported unsolved nodes. Static circuit/placement are clean; routing is the remaining issue.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n\n- Confusing/surprising: built-in USB-C works with default routing, but `sequential_trace` failed because it wanted an explicit connector footprint.\n- Wasted most time: iterating tiny courtyard/placement issues and then waiting on autorouter failures after clean placement.\n- Helpful changes: clearer footprint-string docs, especially for crystals; clearer distinction between DRC warnings, placement checker output, and fatal build errors.\n- Friction points: `tsci build --output` is unsupported; React `key` warnings appear for mapped traces; autorouter failure reports node IDs but not the source `<trace>` names.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019e8ead-3fdb-77d3-a78e-cef14bcae7bf","turnId":"019e8ead-3fee-7a90-8564-fe53b81ce8f4","completedAtMs":1780511288452}}
